      "body": "## Bevy 0.8-dev\r\n\r\n## What you did\r\n\r\nMy terrain renderer is streaming in and out 1000 of textures per minute and after a while the application slows down. At first I thought there had to be a memory leak somewhere, but this did not seem to be the case. After profiling I have noticed that after a while the asset loading system takes up tones of frame time. Notice the turquoise system taking over. This issue only occurs when I have watch_for_changes enabled.\r\n\r\nWatch for changes seems to track unloaded assets as well. \r\nIs there a way of activating hot reloading only for shaders but not for images?\r\n\r\n## What went wrong\r\n\r\nThe asset server takes increasingly longer after I am streaming (loading and unloading) assets for a while.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nHere some images of the profiling I have been doing.\r\n\r\nProblematic frame\r\n![](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/866787577687310356/980786494300127292/unknown.png)\r\n\r\nNormal frame (shortly after startup)\r\n![](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/866787577687310356/980788126341541958/Screenshot_2022-05-30_at_12-34-00_trace-1653906302.json_830_MB_-_Perfetto_UI.png)\r\n\r\nThe turquoise system (assets server) is taking over all of the frame time.\r\n![](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/866787577687310356/981100455788699668/unknown.png)\r\n\r\n",
